    "result_text": "The build passes with all tests green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the direct level-computation rule with a points system.\n\n**`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a new `membershipPoints` field to the Owner schema and rewrote the `membershipLevel` description to reflect that it's now derived from points.\n\n**`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `membershipPoints` mapping/method and rewrote `membershipLevel`:\n\n- `membershipPoints(owner)`: starts at 0; `+2` when an email is present; `+1` when `namesakeCount == 0`; `+2` when `householdSize >= 3`; `+3` when tenure exceeds 365 days.\n- `membershipLevel(owner)`: maps points to level \u2192 `1` (0\u20131), `2` (2\u20133), `3` (4\u20135), `4` (6+).\n\nBoth fields are now returned on the Owner DTO (`OwnerDto` is code-generated from the OpenAPI spec, so adding the schema field gives it a setter that the MapStruct mapping populates).\n\nThe acceptance test's scenario (fresh owner with email, no namesake, single-member household, zero tenure) scores 2 + 1 = 3 points \u2192 level 2, matching the expected `membershipPoints=3` / `membershipLevel=2`. `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
