    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered sequence of what happens when you `POST /api/owners`, from the code as it currently stands.\n\n## Phase 1 \u2014 Before the controller body runs\n\n1. **Security / method authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")` on `addOwner` requires role `ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN`. (Only enforced when `petclinic.security.enable=true`; the `DisableSecurityConfig` profile does not enable method security, so it's a no-op there.)\n2. **Bean Validation on the request body** (`OwnerFieldsDto`, via `@Valid`), fails \u2192 `400` through `ExceptionControllerAdvice`:\n   - `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (letters, up to 3 words with space/apostrophe/hyphen)\n   - `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (same, optional trailing `.`)\n   - `address` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..255)`, `@Pattern(.*\\S.*)` (non-blank)\n   - `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`, non-blank\n   - `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`, non-blank\n   - `postcode` (optional) \u2014 `@Pattern(^[0-9]{4}$)`\n   - `email` (optional) \u2014 `@Email`, `@Size(max 255)`\n\n## Phase 2 \u2014 Manual validations & normalizations inside `addOwner` (in this exact order)\n\n3. **Email** (`normalizeEmail`) \u2014 blank \u2192 null; otherwise lower-case, must match `EMAIL_PATTERN`, and must **not** be a disposable domain (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`). Invalid \u2192 `400`. Normalized value written back.\n4. **Postcode** (`normalizePostcode`) \u2014 blank \u2192 null; otherwise must be 4 digits, and if the city is a known region (`CITY_REGION`), must fall in that region's range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099). Invalid \u2192 `400`.\n5. **Address** (`normalizeAddress`) \u2014 trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand `ST/RD/AVE`; if result is blank \u2192 `400`. Normalized value written back.\n6. **City capacity** (`countOwnersInCity`) \u2014 if the city already has **\u2265 50** owners \u2192 `409 CONFLICT`. *(Full owner table read.)*\n7. **Telephone \u2192 E.164** (`toE164`) \u2014 strip separators, default country code `+61`, enforce 8\u201315 digits plus per-country length. Cannot form a valid number \u2192 `400`. Normalized value written back.\n8. **Map DTO \u2192 `Owner` entity** (`ownerMapper.toOwner`).\n9. **Identity duplicate** (`identityContact` = `telephone|email`) \u2014 if any existing owner shares that key \u2192 `409 CONFLICT`. *(Full table read.)*\n10. **Household duplicate** (`ownerMapper.householdId` = SHA-256 of `lastName|postcode`) \u2014 if a household already exists **and** `sharesHousehold` is not `true` \u2192 `409 CONFLICT`. *(Full table read.)* If it exists and `sharesHousehold` is true, the owner is flagged as a declared member.\n11. **Registration date** \u2014 default to today if absent; a **future** date \u2192 `400`; then rolled forward to the next business day (`toBusinessDay`).\n12. **Daily sign-up limit** (`countOwnersRegisteredOn`) \u2014 if **\u2265 100** owners already registered on that business day \u2192 `429 TOO_MANY_REQUESTS`. *(Full table read.)*\n\n## Phase 3 \u2014 Derived fields set on the entity (side-effects, computed before save)\n\n13. `registrationDate` \u2014 set to the (possibly rolled-forward) date.\n14. `customerCode` \u2014 derived from region + SHA-256 hash (`customerCode`).\n15. `namesakeCount` \u2014 count of existing owners with the same first+last name (`countNamesakes`, full table read).\n16. `bulkSignupWarning` \u2014 `true` if **> 80** owners registered on that business day (another full table read).\n17. `householdSize` \u2014 count of household members + 1 (`countHouseholdMembers`, full table read).\n18. `possibleDuplicate` / `possibleDuplicateOf` \u2014 if declared member, forced to `false`/`null`; otherwise a soft-match search (`findPossibleDuplicate`) sets the flag and matched id.\n\n## Phase 4 \u2014 Persistence and its own validation\n\n19. **`clinicService.saveOwner(owner)`** \u2014 `@Transactional` write boundary \u2192 `ownerRepository.save(owner)` (Spring Data JPA).\n20. **Entity-level Bean Validation at JPA flush** (Hibernate re-validates before INSERT): `Owner.address`/`city` `@NotEmpty`; `telephone` `@NotEmpty` + `@Pattern(^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$)`; `Person.firstName`/`lastName` `@NotEmpty`. `pets` is `cascade=ALL` but none are attached here. No `@PrePersist`/lifecycle callbacks or published events exist.\n\n## Phase 5 \u2014 Response side-effects\n\n21. **Audit log** \u2014 `AUDIT.info(\"owner created id=\u2026 customerCode=\u2026 registrationDate=\u2026 membershipLevel=\u2026\")` (membership level computed by the mapper for the log line only).\n22. **Map `Owner` \u2192 `OwnerDto`** for the body (computes display/derived fields).\n23. **`Location` header** set to `/api/owners/{id}`, response returned as **`201 CREATED`**.\n\n---\n\nA couple of things worth flagging from reading the code:\n\n- Steps 6, 9, 10, 12, 15, 16, 17, 18 each issue **separate full-table reads** via `findAllOwners()` \u2014 the create path scans the entire owners table many times.\n- The manual `toE164` (step 7) is what makes the telephone satisfy the entity's `@Pattern` in step 20; the two are only consistent because of that normalization.\n\nOne note: the code above was gathered partly from `target/generated-sources/openapi/\u2026` (the generated OpenAPI interface/DTO). That's build output, but it's the actual source of the `@Valid` body constraints and the route mapping, so it's accurate to the current state. I did not modify anything."
